    "evidence": "The headline, 85% result, and deployment decision clearly communicate that this is a post-remediation regression—not an independent holdout—and therefore not production-ready. However, the required next action is only stated as prose: there is no visible control to create, schedule, or inspect an independent holdout. The most prominent action, “Hide scope evidence,” instead collapses the proof. Dense low-contrast microcopy and the mobile header’s clipped navigation further weaken scanability and orientation.",
